    "question": "Toby is counting goldfish in the local pond. He knows that only 25% of goldfish are at the surface and the rest are too deep below the surface to be able to see. If he counts 15 goldfish, how many are below the surface?",
    "gold": "45",
    "answer": "There are 60 goldfish because 15 / .25 = <<15/.25=60>>60\n75% of the fish are below the surface because 100 - 25 = <<100-25=75>>75\nThere are 45 goldfish below the surface because 60 x .75 = <<60*.75=45>>45\n#### 45"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many goldfish are below the surface, we start by understanding the given information and breaking it down step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of goldfish Toby counted:**\n   Toby counted 15 goldfish.\n\n2. **Determine the percentage of goldfish at the surface:**\n   Toby knows that only 25% of the goldfish are at the surface. This means that 75% of the goldfish are below the surface.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of goldfish below the surface:**\n   To find the number of goldfish below the surface, we need to calculate 75% of the total number of goldfish Toby counted. We can do this by multiplying 15 by 75% (or 0.75 in decimal form):\n   \\[\n   15 \\times 0.75 = 11.25\n   \\]\n   Since the number of goldfish must be a whole number, we round 11.25 to the nearest whole number, which is 11.\n\nTherefore, the number of goldfish below the surface is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).",
